# Repo-level rule suppression (keur ADR-035), same pattern as keur and loods.
#
# VAULT-PERSONAL fires on the owner's GitHub handle in the repo URLs and the
# author field. In this
# public package that is authorship, not a leak (keur ADR-043). It is a
# personal-vault rule from the global ~/.config/keur/rules/ layer, meant for
# the personal notes vault. Scoping it off here is a scope correction, not a bypass.
VAULT-PERSONAL

# VAULT-WORK fires on the owner's name in package.json `author`. In a public npm
# package that is authorship, not a leak; keur's own .keurignore scopes it off for
# the same reason (keur ADR-043).
VAULT-WORK

# VAULT-GDPR_NL scans prose for GDPR/PII terms; here it only hits third-party
# metadata in package-lock.json. That is a false positive on upstream data, not
# personal data.
VAULT-GDPR_NL
